# RunPod safety

## Read-only default

List pods, endpoints, templates, GPU types, workers, jobs, volumes, and billing
are fine when RunPod work is authorized. Do **not**:

- create or update a pod / endpoint / template / network volume
- start, stop, restart, or delete a pod
- delete an endpoint or purge its queue
- cancel or retry a job
- create or delete container-registry auth

…unless the user gave an explicit verb this turn naming the object (or clear
create intent with required fields).

## Cost and secrets

Before create/start: state that GPU time bills while running. Prefer scale-to-zero
or stop when idle if the user did not ask to leave it up. Never paste API keys,
registry passwords, or env secret values into chat — refuse dumps
(`security-secrets` posture).
